---
// The claims: what people have said about merging with machines, in date order, beside what the
// seven branches have actually reached, so a reader sees the gap between talk and delivery
// (tracker pattern, rule 6.4, ruled by John 2026-10-16). Every claim comes from data/claims/
// through scripts/export.py; the delivery column comes from tree.json and bandwidth.json.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { tree, claims, bandwidth, longDate, hostOf, REPO } from '../lib/tree';

const c = tree.counts;
const k = claims.counts;
const list = claims.claims;
const first = list[0]?.when.slice(0, 4);
const last = list[list.length - 1]?.when.slice(0, 4);
const text = bandwidth.measures.find((m) => m.key === 'text');
const speech = text?.baselines.find((b) => b.id === 'speech-in-conversation');
const textBest = text?.best ? text.points.find((p) => p.id === text.best!.id) : null;
const plural = c.first_human_or_beyond === 1;
---

<Base title="The claims — The Upgrade Tree" description="What people have said about humans merging with machines, each on a dated occasion with the recording or text it can be checked against, set beside what the seven branches of The Upgrade Tree have actually reached.">
  <section class="hero wide">
    <p class="eyebrow">The claims</p>
    <h1>What people have claimed, beside what has been done</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      {k.claims} claims by {k.speakers} people, {first} to {last}, oldest first, each one checked against the
      recording or the text. On the right, what the seven branches have actually reached. The two never mix: a claim
      moves nothing on the tree, and nothing on the tree makes a claim true.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section explain narrow">
    <p>
      A <em>claim</em>, here, is one person saying one thing about humans merging with or upgrading themselves by
      machines, on one dated occasion: a talk, an interview, a book, a post. It is not a summary of what someone
      thinks in general. Each entry names who spoke and when, links the recording or the original text with the
      timestamp or page, and says how the words were checked (listened to, an official transcript, machine-made
      captions, or the published text). It quotes <em>at most one short phrase</em>, in quotation marks, exactly as
      it is in the source; everything else is in our own words, with the speaker's hedges and conditions kept,
      because a hedge is part of what was claimed. When a sentence circulates as a quote and the recording has
      different words or none, the entry says so and shows what differs. When only a reporter's account of a remark
      exists, the entry is held as <em>unsourced, coverage only</em>, carries no quoted words, and names the reporter.
      Critics of the merger idea are entered on the same terms as its advocates.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="claims-grid">
    <div class="claims-list">
      <div class="shead">
        <h2>The talk: {k.claims} claims</h2>
        <span>{k.sourced} sourced, {k.unsourced} held on coverage only, {k.critics} from critics</span>
      </div>
      <ol class="claims">
        {list.map((cl) => (
          <li id={cl.id} class={`claim ${cl.status} ${cl.critic ? 'critic' : ''}`}>
            <header class="claim-head">
              <p class="claim-when">
                <a href={`#${cl.id}`}>{cl.when_label}</a>
                {cl.released_on && <span class="dim"> · published {longDate(cl.released_on)}</span>}
              </p>
              <p class="claim-who">
                <strong>{cl.speaker}</strong>{cl.role && <span class="dim">, {cl.role}</span>}
              </p>
              <p class="claim-where">{cl.occasion}</p>
              <p class="chips">
                {cl.critic && <span class="chip accent">a critic's entry</span>}
                {cl.status === 'unsourced' && <span class="chip no">unsourced: coverage only</span>}
                {cl.paraphrase && !cl.paraphrase.primary_found && <span class="chip no">a circulating version has no primary source</span>}
                {cl.verify.length > 0 && <span class="chip">still to check</span>}
              </p>
            </header>

            {cl.words ? (
              <blockquote class="claim-words">
                <p>“{cl.words}”</p>
                {cl.words_locator && <footer>{cl.words_locator}</footer>}
              </blockquote>
            ) : (
              <p class="claim-nowords">
                No words are quoted. This entry rests on a reporter's account, which is coverage, not the speaker's own
                words, so it is held as unsourced.
              </p>
            )}

            <p class="claim-text"><strong>{cl.status === 'sourced' ? 'What was claimed.' : 'What was reported.'}</strong> {cl.claimed}</p>
            {cl.not_in_source && <p class="claim-text"><strong>Not in the source.</strong> {cl.not_in_source}</p>}

            <p class="claim-source">
              <strong>Where to check.</strong>{' '}
              <a href={cl.source_url} rel="noopener">{hostOf(cl.source_url)}</a>{cl.source_locator && <>, {cl.source_locator}</>}.{' '}
              <span class="dim">How the words were checked: {cl.checked_how}</span>
            </p>
            {cl.ruling && <p class="claim-ruling">{cl.ruling}</p>}

            {cl.paraphrase && (
              <div class="claim-para">
                <p><strong>{cl.paraphrase.primary_found ? 'A version that circulates.' : 'A version that circulates, with no primary source found.'}</strong></p>
                <p><span class="k">Repeated as</span> {cl.paraphrase.repeated}</p>
                <p><span class="k">Seen</span> {cl.paraphrase.seen}</p>
                <p><span class="k">What differs</span> {cl.paraphrase.differs}</p>
              </div>
            )}

            {cl.bears_on.length > 0 && (
              <p class="claim-bears">
                <span class="k">Bears on</span>{' '}
                {cl.bears_on.map((b, i) => (
                  <><a href={b.path} class={b.kind === 'upgrade' ? 'bears-upgrade' : 'bears-branch'}>{b.name}</a>{i < cl.bears_on.length - 1 ? '; ' : ''}</>
                ))}
                {cl.bears_on_note && <span class="dim"> ({cl.bears_on_note})</span>}
              </p>
            )}

            <details class="claim-more">
              <summary>The source in full, the coverage, and the notes</summary>
              <p><span class="k">Primary source</span> {cl.source}</p>
              {cl.when_note && <p><span class="k">On the date</span> {cl.when_note}</p>}
              {cl.coverage.length > 0 && (
                <p><span class="k">Coverage</span> {cl.coverage.join(' ')}</p>
              )}
              {cl.why_here && <p><span class="k">Why it is here</span> {cl.why_here}</p>}
              {cl.notes && <p><span class="k">Notes</span> {cl.notes}</p>}
              {cl.verify.length > 0 && (
                <p><span class="k">Still to check</span> {cl.verify.join(' ')}</p>
              )}
              <p class="dim">This entry is <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/${cl.file}`} rel="noopener">{cl.file}</a> in the public repository.</p>
            </details>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </div>

    <aside class="claims-side">
      <div class="side-card delivered">
        <h3>The delivery: what has actually been done</h3>
        <p class="big-number">{c.first_human_or_beyond}<small>of {c.upgrades}</small></p>
        <p class="delivered-claim">
          {plural ? 'way' : 'ways'} of changing a human being on purpose {plural ? 'has' : 'have'} been tried in at least one living person, counted from the public record.
        </p>
        <ul class="delivered-branches">
          {tree.branches.map((b) => (
            <li>
              <a href={b.path}>{b.name}</a>
              <span class={`stage-badge stage-${b.furthest_rank ?? 'none'}`}><i aria-hidden="true"></i>{b.furthest_label ? b.furthest_label.toLowerCase() : 'nothing recorded'}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <p class="delivered-note">Each branch is shown at the furthest stage any upgrade under it has reached. <a href="/branches/">The branches</a> have the full list.</p>
      </div>
      {textBest && speech && (
        <div class="side-card">
          <h3>The number the claims rest on</h3>
          <p>
            The fastest a brain has yet talked to a machine is <strong>{textBest.value} {textBest.unit}</strong>
            of decoded attempted speech, reported on {longDate(textBest.date)}. Speech in conversation runs at about
            {' '}{speech.value} {speech.unit}. <a href="/branches/link/#bandwidth">The whole series, with its sources.</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      )}
      <div class="side-card">
        <h3>Disagree with something</h3>
        <p>A claim missing, a date wrong, a phrase misquoted, a hedge dropped. <a href="/disagree/">Say so.</a></p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <section class="section narrow prose" id="not-entered">
    <h2>Looked for and not found</h2>
    {claims.not_entered.checked.map((x) => (
      <p>
        <strong>{x.who}</strong>{x.role && <>, {x.role}</>}. {x.result} What was checked: {x.checked}
      </p>
    ))}

    <h2>Noted, not yet checked</h2>
    <p class="dim" style="font-size: 15px;">Occasions that may belong on this page once the recording or text has been reached. Nothing here is a claim yet.</p>
    <ul class="to-add">
      {claims.not_entered.to_add.map((x) => <li>{x.lead} <span class="dim">{x.status}</span></li>)}
    </ul>

    <p class="dim" style="font-size: 14px; margin-top: 24px;">
      The record itself is one file per claim in <a href={`${REPO}/tree/main/data/claims`} rel="noopener">data/claims</a> in the public repository; the rules are in <a href="/method/">how the numbers are worked out</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
